CORE
arithmetic.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ multiplication: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ division: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ addition: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ subtraction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ expected to fail: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Floating-point arithmetic is encoded as bit-vector operations with lots of
shared sub-expressions, which are defined as separate SMT functions.
